# p_a1b2 — Standard split: Elena commutes, Priya home, dog by Elena

Elena leaves for her office around 8:00 on weekdays and returns at 17:30. Her laptop, backpack, wallet, hat, helmet, bike lock, and umbrella all go out with her. Priya is home most of the day, takes a morning walk 7:00–8:00, and runs afternoon errands 14:00–16:00. The dog is fed by Priya at 7:30 (bowl at the kitchen floor) and walked by Elena in the evening 18:00–19:00. Meals are at the dining table: lunch 12:00–13:30, dinner 18:30–20:00. Evening TV runs 20:00–22:30 with the remote, blanket, and fruit bowl on the coffee table. Priya plays guitar in the bedroom 21:00–22:00. Elena bakes on Saturday mornings 9:00–12:00. Priya showers 6:30–7:30; Elena showers 21:30–22:30.

What sets this hypothesis apart: the entry hook is bare of Elena's cycling gear between 8:00 and 17:30 on weekdays, and the dining table holds plates and glasses only during meal windows. What would refute it: Elena's laptop sighted in the house between 9:00 and 17:00 on a weekday, or the dog bowl still full on the kitchen floor at 18:00 (implying Elena fed it, not Priya).

